1
00:00:00,152 --> 00:00:01,040
If you stuck a needle

2
00:00:01,080 --> 00:00:02,600
into a DEAD spider…

3
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:04,520
you could make its legs MOVE again.

4
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:05,960
Because when a spider dies,

5
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,800
all its legs curl inward.

6
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:09,720
You see, spiders use fluid pressure

7
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:10,960
to straighten their legs.

8
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:11,987
And when they die,

9
00:00:12,027 --> 00:00:13,480
that pressure disappears.

10
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:15,200
So scientists attached a syringe

11
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:16,467
to a dead spider…

12
00:00:16,507 --> 00:00:18,120
and pumped air inside.

13
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:20,070
Its legs suddenly spread OPEN.

14
00:00:20,110 --> 00:00:21,630
But when they released the pressure…

15
00:00:21,670 --> 00:00:23,390
the legs CLAMPED SHUT.

16
00:00:23,430 --> 00:00:24,720
They'd turned a dead spider

17
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:26,170
into a working claw.

18
00:00:26,210 --> 00:00:27,320
And they actually used it

19
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:28,253
to pick up…

20
00:00:28,293 --> 00:00:29,600
ANOTHER dead spider.

